  "problem": "$(7+\\sqrt{-27})-(4-\\sqrt{-12})=$",
  "worked_solution": "Given the complex number $a+b\\,\\text{i},$ $a$ represents its real part while $b$ represents its imaginary part.\n\nTo add or subtract complex numbers, we add or subtract their real parts, and we add or subtract their imaginary parts.\n\nFor the given problem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(7+\\sqrt{-27})-(4-\\sqrt{-12}) & =(7+\\sqrt{9\\cdot 3}\\,\\text{i})-(4-\\sqrt{4\\cdot 3}\\,\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(7+3\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i})-(4-2\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(7-4)+(3\\sqrt{3}-(-2\\sqrt{3}))\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =3+(3\\sqrt{3}+2\\sqrt{3})\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =3+5\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
